From: Tomaz Zaman <tomaz@mono.si>
Subject: [PATCH] cfg80211: set_monitor_channel gained its netdev in 6.12, not 6.13

The driver adds the struct net_device * argument to .set_monitor_channel
only from 6.13, but the prototype changed in 6.12:

  4dae80dd259b ("wifi: cfg80211: pass net_device to .set_monitor_channel")
  authored 2024-10-09, released in v6.12

Building against a native 6.12 cfg80211 therefore assigns a function of the
wrong type into cfg80211_ops and fails:

  moal_sta_cfg80211.c:524:32: error: initialization of
  'int (*)(struct wiphy *, struct net_device *, struct cfg80211_chan_def *)'
  from incompatible pointer type
  'int (*)(struct wiphy *, struct cfg80211_chan_def *)'

This does not show up in builds that use the backports package, because
there CFG80211_VERSION_CODE reports the backport's own base version rather
than the running kernel's, and that base predates the change. Comparing
against 6.12.0 is right for both: a backport older than 6.12 still selects
the old signature.

Upstream-Status: Pending [sent to NXP; the guard is wrong for any native
6.12 cfg80211, not only for this build]

Signed-off-by: Tomaz Zaman <tomaz@mono.si>
---
 mlinux/moal_sta_cfg80211.c | 4 ++--
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

--- a/mlinux/moal_sta_cfg80211.c
+++ b/mlinux/moal_sta_cfg80211.c
@@ -127,7 +127,7 @@
 #ifdef UAP_SUPPORT
 #if CFG80211_VERSION_CODE >= KERNEL_VERSION(3, 8, 0)
 static int woal_cfg80211_set_monitor_channel(struct wiphy *wiphy,
-#if CFG80211_VERSION_CODE >= KERNEL_VERSION(6, 13, 0)
+#if CFG80211_VERSION_CODE >= KERNEL_VERSION(6, 12, 0)
 					     struct net_device *dev,
 #endif
 					     struct cfg80211_chan_def *chandef);
@@ -699,7 +699,7 @@
 #ifdef UAP_SUPPORT
 #if CFG80211_VERSION_CODE >= KERNEL_VERSION(3, 8, 0)
 static int woal_cfg80211_set_monitor_channel(struct wiphy *wiphy,
-#if CFG80211_VERSION_CODE >= KERNEL_VERSION(6, 13, 0)
+#if CFG80211_VERSION_CODE >= KERNEL_VERSION(6, 12, 0)
 					     struct net_device *dev,
 #endif
 					     struct cfg80211_chan_def *chandef)
